From 1677e8ebc1b33b69059ad5226b32bc6031c6af8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 14:36:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(landing): App Store + Play Store badges, Sign in nav,
 dedicated /pricing page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses three pieces of Doc's feedback after PR 1:

1. Sign in / Sign up surfaced on the landing page.
   - New TopNav now has "Sign in" (text link → /login) and "Sign up free"
     (pill button → scrolls to #get-the-app store badges).
   - Hero also has a "Already have an account? Sign in →" secondary link.
   - No /register route exists on web — sign-up happens inside the iOS /
     Android app on first launch — so the "Sign up free" button intentionally
     scrolls to the download badges rather than a non-existent web form.

2. App Store and Google Play are now visually separated as official store
   badges. Replaces every previous "App Store" pill button (which was a
   misleading single-CTA that linked only to Apple). New <StoreBadges />
   component renders both badges side-by-side, used in:
     - Hero (large)
     - Final CTA section (large, centered)
   Also fixes the "Android coming soon" line — Android has been live for a
   while; updated copy to "Free to download on iOS and Android."

3. Pricing removed from the landing page entirely (per Doc's "should not
   show any subscriptions, mimic the app"). Subscriptions are sold inside
   the app via the App Store / Play Store IAP flow; the landing page just
   gets people to the download. Cleaner, less to maintain, no risk of
   drift between the landing page and the actual store prices.

4. New /pricing public route at frontend/src/landing/PricingPage.jsx.
   - Three-tier comparison: Free + Heritage Keeper + Legacy Collection
     ("Most popular"). Sourced from frontend/src/subscription.js (the
     in-app PricingPage) so both stay aligned.
   - Monthly / Annual toggle.
   - Each tier ends with both store badges (subscribers buy in-app).
   - FAQ block answering the standard subscription questions (where
     billed, how to cancel, family sharing, what's an AI credit, do
     prices change).
   - In dev only (NODE_ENV !== "production"), renders a yellow banner
     reminding the team to verify the PRICES const against actual Play
     Console / App Store Connect numbers — Doc flagged that the
     subscription.js prices may not match what's live, and this banner
     keeps the TODO visible until the canonical source is confirmed.
   - Logged-in users get redirected to /subscribe (the in-app upgrade
     page), so /pricing serves only prospective/anonymous visitors.

5. App.js routes /pricing -> PublicPricingPage. The existing in-app
   PricingPage from ./subscription.js is unchanged and still routes from
   /subscribe (ProtectedRoute, requires login).

Not in this PR (intentional):
- Verifying the actual store prices (Doc to confirm; one-line PRICES
  edit when known).
- Extracting shared <StoreBadges /> and tier data into a /landing/shared/
  module — both landing pages currently duplicate them. Worth doing if a
  third page needs the badges.
- Replacing the founder-photo placeholder with a real photo (PR 3).
- Terms of Service page (PR 3).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
